					"Weak-Willed", "Whimsy", "Witch-Hunted",
				},
				-- The two COMBAT lists, 13th batch (SPEC I157c, T1006, user 2026-09-07). 189 weapons
				-- and manoeuvres and 33 pieces of armour, generated from research/weapon.tsv and
				-- research/armor.tsv by research/gen_combat_data.ps1 - the SAME tables combatData.lua
				-- and the four desc modules come out of, so a name here without a measured row there
				-- cannot happen (SPEC V456f, the shape V454 already holds the backgrounds to).
				--
				-- Canonical ENGLISH, because that is what the sheet saves (SPEC V24); the PT map and
				-- the .lang carry one key per name. Four books: V20 core, M20, W20 and V20 Dark Ages
				-- (SPEC R149, Q77.1) - the Victorian Age, the Dark Ages Companion and the Garou-form
				-- manoeuvres stayed out, and so did the nine Do techniques (SPEC R150, V456d).
				--
				-- The suffix vocabulary is the CLOSED one of I105e(1) - (Mage), (Werewolf),
				-- (Dark Ages) - plus `, Thrown`, which is the book's own spelling for a weapon that
				-- appears in both the melee and the throwing table of one book. A name repeats only
				-- when a cell differs; same name and same cells is ONE entry, from the book with the
				-- higher precedence, core > m20 > w20 > da (SPEC R151).
				["weapon"] = {
					"", ".30 Caliber Machine Gun", ".50 Caliber Machine Gun", "30 mm Cannon", "3-Round Burst", "Aiming",
