				-- The four SHIELDS live in a list of their own so the ARMOR box cannot offer one and
				-- the SHIELD box cannot offer a jacket - a character wears both at once, which is
				-- the whole point of the box (SPEC I159a, I159b, user 2026-09-07). Only the LIST
				-- splits: combatData.armor still holds all thirty-three and descArmor_* still
				-- describes all thirty-three, because a shield reads the same columns an armour
				-- does. The split is driven by the `kind` column of research/armor.tsv, so nothing
				-- here is hand-picked, and V466c measures that the two lists never overlap.
